# WEBrick logged whatever it is handed: BasicLog#format returned
# arg.message and arg.to_str verbatim, and every string that reached a
# logger call went to the log device with its control characters intact
# (CWE-117). The exploitable flow is HTTP Basic authentication, where a
# username decoded straight from the Authorization header is interpolated
# into an error message:
#
#   lib/webrick/httpauth/basicauth.rb
#     userid, password = basic_credentials.unpack("m*")[0].split(":", 2)
#     unless encpass = @userdb.get_passwd(@realm, userid, @reload_db)
#       error("%s: the user is not allowed.", userid)
#
# and the Authenticator module turns that into a log write:
#
#   lib/webrick/httpauth/authenticator.rb
#     def log(meth, fmt, *args)
#       msg = format("%s %s: ", @auth_scheme, @realm)
#       msg << fmt % args
#       @logger.send(meth, msg)
#     end
#
# The fixed revision wraps both branches of BasicLog#format in AccessLog.escape
# and removes the older escape from HTTPStatus::Status#initialize, so escaping
# now happens once, at the log boundary, for plain strings as well as
# exceptions. The regression test drives a "foo\ebar" username and asserts
# the log carries no escape sequence.
#
# Held, and the flow is blocked at three independent points, each isolated
# by a probe that holds the other two constant:
#
# 1. No source. `req[@request_field]` (authenticator.rb:73) is a subscript
#    read on the request parameter; `vyql match` on basicauth.rb and on
#    authenticator.rb reports no source label at all -- the only labels in
#    basicauth.rb are DynamicCodeLoad on its three `require` lines. A
#    binding would have to key on the parameter's name.
# 2. The message assembly loses the taint. `msg << fmt % args` in statement
#    position propagates nothing to its receiver while the same call in
#    expression position carries its argument's taint through the result --
#    the third and fourth test below are that minimal pair. The lowering
#    models `<<` as a call whose result is the only tainted output, so fixing
#    it means a receiver-mutation relation for every Ruby String/Array/IO
#    append, which is not a localized correction.
# 3. No sink. `@logger.send(meth, msg)` (authenticator.rb:88) labels
#    nothing: holding a labelled source and expression-position assembly
#    fixed and varying only the sink spelling reports 1 through the bare
#    `logger.error` receiver and 0 through `send` -- the third and fifth
#    test below are that pair. Object#send on a config-injected logger is
#    not a documented logging API, and widening the receiver-qualified
#    logger spellings was measured in the first review and reverted: across
#    the whole tree it fired exactly one finding, filehandler.rb:342's
#    `@logger.warn("the request refers nondisclosure name
#    `#{File.basename(res.filename)}'.")`, identically at the vulnerable and
#    the patched revision (the fix does not touch that file), while adding
#    19 medium log rows of ordinary `@logger.info("... #{env[:x]} ...")`
#    operational logging on one 867-file subtree (97 to 116 findings).
#
# Fresh 3 x --cache off scans of both revisions report the same 47 findings
# (47/47/47 and 47/47/47), no VYQL-INJ-009 on either, and nothing at all on
# basicauth.rb, authenticator.rb or accesslog.rb in either the findings
# report or the flags view.
#
# The neutraliser half is a needle miss, not a token miss. WEBrick's escape
# is `data.gsub(/[[:cntrl:]\\]+/) {$&.dump[1...-1]}.untaint`
# (accesslog.rb:153), and logEscape342's needle is `[[:cntrl:]]`, which the
# character class `[[:cntrl:]\\]` does not contain -- after its first `]`
# comes a backslash, not a second `]`. A Ruby regex-literal argument *is*
# exposed as an `args.any.literal` token: `data.gsub(/[[:cntrl:]]+/)
# {...}` labels core.LogEscape today, as does the same call with a string
# pattern. The site is labelled, as threat.CharFilter by the generic
# `call.filter.global` binding, so widening the needle to the POSIX class
# prefix would label it -- and move no finding anywhere: across the whole
# clone pool the control-char gsub idiom occurs in three projects -- here,
# rack, and two shirasagi scraper and sanitiser sites that no logger call
# reads -- no log finding reaches either revision, and the in-place `gsub!`
# spelling that carries dominance coverage does not occur here at all.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-engine-gap, both revisions rejected;
# when receiver-mutating `<<` propagates, the fourth test must flip to
# expect VYQL-INJ-009, and when a logger sink resolves `send`, the fifth
# must.

test "rank1944: the basic auth username reaches the log unescaped"
  lang ruby
  file lib/webrick/httpauth/basicauth.rb
  reject VYQL-INJ-009
  code
  ```
  module WEBrick
    module HTTPAuth
      module Authenticator
        def check_scheme(req)
          unless credentials = req[@request_field]
            error("no credentials in the request.")
            return nil
          end
          match = /^#{@auth_scheme}\s+/i.match(credentials)
          match.post_match
        end

        def error(fmt, *args)
          if @logger.error?
            log(:error, fmt, *args)
          end
        end

        def log(meth, fmt, *args)
          msg = format("%s %s: ", @auth_scheme, @realm)
          msg << fmt % args
          @logger.send(meth, msg)
        end
      end

      class BasicAuth
        include Authenticator

        def authenticate(req, res)
          unless basic_credentials = check_scheme(req)
            challenge(req, res)
          end
          userid, password = basic_credentials.unpack("m*")[0].split(":", 2)
          password ||= ""
          unless encpass = @userdb.get_passwd(@realm, userid, @reload_db)
            error("%s: the user is not allowed.", userid)
            challenge(req, res)
          end
          req.user = userid
        end

        def challenge(req, res)
          raise Unauthorized
        end
      end
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1944: the fixed revision escapes every logged value at the log boundary"
  lang ruby
  file lib/webrick/log.rb
  reject VYQL-INJ-009
  code
  ```
  module WEBrick
    class BasicLog
      def error(msg)
        log(ERROR, "ERROR " << format(msg))
      end

      def log(level, data)
        if @log && level <= @level
          data += "\n" if /\n\Z/ !~ data
          @log << data
        end
      end

      def format(arg)
        if arg.is_a?(Exception)
          "#{arg.class}: #{AccessLog.escape(arg.message)}\n\t" <<
          arg.backtrace.join("\n\t") << "\n"
        elsif arg.respond_to?(:to_str)
          AccessLog.escape(arg.to_str)
        else
          arg.inspect
        end
      end
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1944: the message assembled in expression position is reported"
  lang ruby
  file lib/webrick/httpauth/authenticator.rb
  expect VYQL-INJ-009
  code
  ```
  module WEBrick
    module HTTPAuth
      module Authenticator
        def log(fmt, *args)
          msg = "WEBrick's realm: " << fmt % args
          logger.error(msg)
        end
      end

      class BasicAuth
        include Authenticator

        def authenticate
          userid = params["authorization"].unpack("m*")[0].split(":", 2)[0]
          unless @userdb.get_passwd(@realm, userid, true)
            log("%s: the user is not allowed.", userid)
          end
        end
      end
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1944: the same append in statement position loses the taint"
  lang ruby
  file lib/webrick/httpauth/authenticator.rb
  reject VYQL-INJ-009
  code
  ```
  module WEBrick
    module HTTPAuth
      module Authenticator
        def log(fmt, *args)
          msg = "WEBrick's realm: "
          msg << fmt % args
          logger.error(msg)
        end
      end

      class BasicAuth
        include Authenticator

        def authenticate
          userid = params["authorization"].unpack("m*")[0].split(":", 2)[0]
          unless @userdb.get_passwd(@realm, userid, true)
            log("%s: the user is not allowed.", userid)
          end
        end
      end
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1944: the same message through the send-dispatched logger is not"
  lang ruby
  file lib/webrick/httpauth/authenticator.rb
  reject VYQL-INJ-009
  code
  ```
  module WEBrick
    module HTTPAuth
      module Authenticator
        def log(meth, fmt, *args)
          msg = "WEBrick's realm: " << fmt % args
          @logger.send(meth, msg)
        end
      end

      class BasicAuth
        include Authenticator

        def authenticate
          userid = params["authorization"].unpack("m*")[0].split(":", 2)[0]
          unless @userdb.get_passwd(@realm, userid, true)
            log(:error, "%s: the user is not allowed.", userid)
          end
        end
      end
    end
  end
  ```
